IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaq-common`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Queensland) -- chapter 7 and chapter 11 part 4 as a claimant meets them:
-- applying to the tribunal (ss 114B, 115), notice of the hearing (s 118), taking part (ss 119, 123, 124), costs (s
-- 127), a declaration about capacity (ss 146, 147), the decision and reasons (ss 156, 158), appeal (ss 163, 164), and
-- reporting abuse, with damages for a reprisal (ss 247, 247A-247C).
--
-- SEAT: the adult whose capacity is in question in the proceeding; for ss 247-247C, a person who reports to an official
-- that an adult is being abused or the Act contravened (who may be the adult). "The tribunal" is QCAT; the QCAT Act,
-- which these sections borrow from, is not deposited and not encoded.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Chapter 7: proceedings about me in the tribunal`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 114B, 115 -- applying, and the fee`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 115(1): "An application may be made, as provided under the QCAT Act, to the tribunal for a declaration, order,
-- direction, recommendation or advice in relation to an adult about something in, or related to, this Act or the Powers
-- of Attorney Act 1998." (2): "by-- (a) the adult concerned; or (b) unless this Act or the Powers of Attorney Act 1998
-- states otherwise--another interested person." s 114B(1): "A fee is not payable to the tribunal for making an
-- application, or filing another document, under this Act." (2): except an appeal to the appeal tribunal under the QCAT
-- Act, ch 2 pt 8 div 1. "interested person" (sch 4): "a person who has a sufficient and genuine concern for the rights
-- and interests of the other person"; whether a person is one may be decided by the tribunal (s 126): asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Who wants to apply` IS ONE OF
    `the adult (me)`
    `an interested person for the adult`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Can I apply to the tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply, and no tribunal fee is payable (ss 114B(1), 115(2)(a))`
    `yes: as an interested person you may apply, unless the Act says otherwise for the order sought, and no tribunal fee is payable (ss 114B(1), 115(2)(b))`
    `no: s 115 lets only the adult or an interested person apply`

GIVEN `who applies` IS A `Who wants to apply`
GIVETH A `Can I apply to the tribunal`
`ss 114B, 115 -- application` `who applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who applies`
    WHEN `the adult (me)` THEN `yes: you may apply, and no tribunal fee is payable (ss 114B(1), 115(2)(a))`
    WHEN `an interested person for the adult` THEN `yes: as an interested person you may apply, unless the Act says otherwise for the order sought, and no tribunal fee is payable (ss 114B(1), 115(2)(b))`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: s 115 lets only the adult or an interested person apply`

@export Can I apply to the tribunal (QCAT) about a guardianship or administration matter, and do I pay a fee (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 114B, 115)?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A `Who wants to apply` @desc Who would apply: you (the adult the application is about); an interested person (someone with a sufficient and genuine concern for the adult's rights and interests); or someone else
GIVETH A `Can I apply to the tribunal`
DECIDE `Can I apply to the tribunal question` IS
    `ss 114B, 115 -- application` `who applies`

GIVEN `it is an appeal to the appeal tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 114B -- no tribunal fee` `it is an appeal to the appeal tribunal` IF
    NOT `it is an appeal to the appeal tribunal`

@export Is my application or document free of a tribunal fee (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 114B)? An appeal to QCAT's appeal tribunal is not covered.
GIVEN `it is an appeal to the appeal tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appeal to QCAT's appeal tribunal (QCAT Act, chapter 2, part 8, division 1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application free question` IS
    `s 114B -- no tribunal fee` `it is an appeal to the appeal tribunal`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 118 -- notice of the hearing to me`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 118(1): "At least 7 days before the hearing of an application about a matter, the tribunal must give notice of the
-- hearing to the adult concerned". (3): not required if the tribunal considers notice "might be prejudicial to the
-- physical or mental health or wellbeing of the adult", or "the adult is evading the hearing", or the adult is
-- unconscious or cannot be located after reasonable inquiries. (5): "the adult's failure to understand the notice does
-- not affect its validity." (6): the tribunal may "(b) reduce the time stated in subsection (1)". (7): "Subject to
-- subsection (3), failure to comply with the requirement to give notice to the adult invalidates a hearing and the
-- tribunal's decision about an application." READINGS: "at least 7 days before" is met by notice given on the hearing
-- day minus 7 or earlier (F2: or 7 clear days, minus 8); a late notice is a failure to comply with the requirement, so
-- s 118(7) reaches it (F9: or only a notice never given). With a reduced time the shorter period is the requirement.
GIVEN `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the days of notice required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 118(1) -- the last day for notice` `the day of the hearing` `the days of notice required` MEANS `the days of notice required` `days before` `the day of the hearing`

@export By what day must the tribunal give me notice of the hearing about me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 118(1))? Use 7 days unless the tribunal has directed a shorter time.
GIVEN `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc The date of the hearing (ISO 8601)
      `the days of notice required` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of notice required: 7, or the shorter time the tribunal directed under s 118(6)(b)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Last day to give me notice of the hearing question` IS
    `s 118(1) -- the last day for notice` `the day of the hearing` `the days of notice required`

DECLARE `Was I given proper notice of the hearing` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you were given notice in time (s 118(1)); it is valid even if you did not understand it (s 118(5))`
    `notice to you was not required: the tribunal considered it prejudicial to you, you were evading the hearing, or you were unconscious or could not be located (s 118(3))`
    `no: you were not given notice in time, so the hearing and the tribunal's decision are invalid (s 118(7))`

GIVEN `notice to me was excused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was given notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was given notice` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the tribunal reduced the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduced number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Was I given proper notice of the hearing`
`s 118 -- notice to the adult` `notice to me was excused` `I was given notice` `the day I was given notice` `the day of the hearing` `the tribunal reduced the time` `the reduced number of days` MEANS
    IF `notice to me was excused`
    THEN `notice to you was not required: the tribunal considered it prejudicial to you, you were evading the hearing, or you were unconscious or could not be located (s 118(3))`
    ELSE IF `I was given notice` AND (`the day I was given notice` `is on or before` (`s 118(1) -- the last day for notice` `the day of the hearing` `the days required`))
         THEN `yes: you were given notice in time (s 118(1)); it is valid even if you did not understand it (s 118(5))`
         ELSE `no: you were not given notice in time, so the hearing and the tribunal's decision are invalid (s 118(7))`
    WHERE
        `the days required` MEANS
            IF `the tribunal reduced the time`
            THEN `the reduced number of days`
            ELSE 7

@export Was I given proper notice of the tribunal hearing about me, and if not, is the decision invalid (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 118(1), (3), (5)-(7))?
GIVEN `notice to me was excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the tribunal consider notice might harm your health or wellbeing, or that you were evading the hearing, or were you unconscious or impossible to locate after reasonable inquiries?
      `I was given notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given notice of the hearing?
      `the day I was given notice` IS A DATE @desc The date you were given notice (ISO 8601); if never, any date
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc The date of the hearing (ISO 8601)
      `the tribunal reduced the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the tribunal direct a shorter notice time than 7 days?
      `the reduced number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc The shorter notice time in days, if the tribunal directed one; otherwise any number
GIVETH A `Was I given proper notice of the hearing`
DECIDE `Was I given proper notice of the hearing question` IS
    `s 118 -- notice to the adult` `notice to me was excused` `I was given notice` `the day I was given notice` `the day of the hearing` `the tribunal reduced the time` `the reduced number of days`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 119, 123, 124, 125 -- taking part`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 119: "Each of the following persons is an active party for a proceeding in relation to an adult-- (a) the adult; (b)
-- if the adult is not the applicant--the applicant; (c) if the proceeding is for the appointment or reappointment of a
-- guardian, administrator or attorney for the adult--the person proposed for appointment or reappointment; (d) any
-- current guardian, administrator or attorney for the adult; (e) the public guardian; (f) the public trustee; (g) a
-- person joined as a party to the proceeding by the tribunal." s 123: "An active party ... may appear in person." s
-- 124(1): "An active party may, with the tribunal's leave, be represented by a lawyer or agent." s 125(1): if the adult
-- "is not represented" the tribunal "may appoint a representative to represent the adult's views, wishes and
-- interests". A closed list: anyone else is not an active party (JUST FALSE).
DECLARE `My part in the proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `the adult the proceeding is about`
    `the applicant`
    `the person proposed for appointment or reappointment`
    `a current guardian, administrator or attorney for the adult`
    `a person the tribunal joined as a party`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Can I take part` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are an active party; you may appear in person, and be represented by a lawyer or agent with the tribunal's leave; if you are not represented the tribunal may appoint a representative for your views, wishes and interests (ss 119(a), 123, 124(1), 125(1))`
    `yes: you are an active party; you may appear in person, and be represented by a lawyer or agent with the tribunal's leave (ss 119, 123, 124(1))`
    `no: you are not an active party; the tribunal may join you as a party (s 119(g))`

GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the proceeding`
GIVETH A `Can I take part`
`ss 119, 123-125 -- active party` `my part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my part`
    WHEN `the adult the proceeding is about` THEN `yes: you are an active party; you may appear in person, and be represented by a lawyer or agent with the tribunal's leave; if you are not represented the tribunal may appoint a representative for your views, wishes and interests (ss 119(a), 123, 124(1), 125(1))`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: you are not an active party; the tribunal may join you as a party (s 119(g))`
    OTHERWISE `yes: you are an active party; you may appear in person, and be represented by a lawyer or agent with the tribunal's leave (ss 119, 123, 124(1))`

@export Am I an active party in the tribunal proceeding, and may I appear and have a lawyer (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 119, 123-125)?
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the proceeding` @desc Your part in the proceeding: the adult it is about; the applicant; the person proposed for appointment; a current guardian, administrator or attorney for the adult; a person the tribunal joined as a party; or someone else
GIVETH A `Can I take part`
DECIDE `Can I take part in the proceeding question` IS
    `ss 119, 123-125 -- active party` `my part`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 127 -- costs`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 127(1): "Each party in a proceeding is to bear the party's own costs of the proceeding." (2): "However, the tribunal
-- may order an applicant to pay an active party's costs and the costs of the tribunal in exceptional circumstances,
-- including, for example, if the tribunal considers the application is frivolous or vexatious." (3): QCAT Act ss 101,
-- 103-109 apply (not deposited, not encoded).
DECLARE `Must I pay costs` IS ONE OF
    `no: each party bears their own costs (s 127(1))`
    `you may have to: as the applicant, the tribunal may order you to pay an active party's costs and the tribunal's costs in exceptional circumstances, such as a frivolous or vexatious application (s 127(2))`

GIVEN `I am the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal considers the circumstances exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I pay costs`
`s 127 -- costs` `I am the applicant` `the tribunal considers the circumstances exceptional` MEANS
    IF `I am the applicant` AND `the tribunal considers the circumstances exceptional`
    THEN `you may have to: as the applicant, the tribunal may order you to pay an active party's costs and the tribunal's costs in exceptional circumstances, such as a frivolous or vexatious application (s 127(2))`
    ELSE `no: each party bears their own costs (s 127(1))`

@export Will I have to pay anyone's costs of the tribunal proceeding (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 127)?
GIVEN `I am the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the applicant in the proceeding?
      `the tribunal considers the circumstances exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal consider there are exceptional circumstances (for example a frivolous or vexatious application)?
GIVETH A `Must I pay costs`
DECIDE `Must I pay costs question` IS
    `s 127 -- costs` `I am the applicant` `the tribunal considers the circumstances exceptional`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 146, 147 -- a declaration about my capacity`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 146(1): "The tribunal may make a declaration about the capacity of an adult, guardian, administrator or attorney
-- for a matter." (2): "on its own initiative or on the application of the individual or another interested person."
-- (3): in deciding whether the individual can communicate decisions, the tribunal "must investigate the use of all
-- reasonable ways of facilitating communication". s 147: "A declaration about whether a person had capacity to enter a
-- contract is, in a subsequent proceeding in which the validity of the contract is in issue, evidence about the person's
-- capacity." For example a release or settlement deed signed when capacity is doubted.
DECLARE `Can I get a declaration about my capacity` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may ask the tribunal to declare your capacity for the matter; it must look at every reasonable way of helping you communicate (s 146(1)-(3))`
    `yes: you may ask the tribunal to declare your capacity to enter the contract; the declaration is evidence of your capacity in a later proceeding about whether the contract is valid (ss 146, 147)`
    `no: only the person concerned or an interested person may apply; the tribunal may still act on its own initiative (s 146(2))`

GIVEN `who applies` IS A `Who wants to apply`
      `the matter is my capacity to enter a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I get a declaration about my capacity`
`ss 146, 147 -- declaration about capacity` `who applies` `the matter is my capacity to enter a contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who applies`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: only the person concerned or an interested person may apply; the tribunal may still act on its own initiative (s 146(2))`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the matter is my capacity to enter a contract`
        THEN `yes: you may ask the tribunal to declare your capacity to enter the contract; the declaration is evidence of your capacity in a later proceeding about whether the contract is valid (ss 146, 147)`
        ELSE `yes: you may ask the tribunal to declare your capacity for the matter; it must look at every reasonable way of helping you communicate (s 146(1)-(3))`

@export Can I ask the tribunal to declare whether I have (or had) capacity for a matter, such as signing a settlement or release, and what use is the declaration (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 146, 147)?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A `Who wants to apply` @desc Who would apply: you (the person whose capacity it is); an interested person for you; or someone else
      `the matter is my capacity to enter a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the declaration about your capacity to enter a contract (for example a settlement or release you signed)?
GIVETH A `Can I get a declaration about my capacity`
DECIDE `Can I get a declaration about my capacity question` IS
    `ss 146, 147 -- declaration about capacity` `who applies` `the matter is my capacity to enter a contract`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 156, 158 -- the decision and the reasons`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 156(2): "as soon as practicable after making its decision, the tribunal must notify, and give a copy of its decision
-- to, each relevant person." (5): if the decision does not include reasons, a written notice that the relevant person may
-- request written reasons (QCAT Act s 122). (7): "relevant person means-- (a) the adult concerned in the matter; or (b)
-- another active party in the proceeding; or (c) another person given notice of the hearing". s 158(3): written reasons
-- go to "(a) the adult concerned in the matter; and (b) each other active party". s 157: the tribunal may postpone this
-- for up to 14 days at a time (s 157(4)), renewable only in exceptional circumstances.
DECLARE `Must I be given the decision` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you must be notified and given a copy of the decision as soon as practicable, and a copy of any written reasons (or told you may ask for them) (ss 156(2), (5), 158(3)); the tribunal may postpone this for up to 14 days at a time (s 157)`
    `yes: you must be notified and given a copy of the decision as soon as practicable, and told you may ask for written reasons if it has none (s 156(2), (5)); you get the reasons themselves only on request (s 158(4))`
    `you are not a relevant person, but you may ask for a copy of the decision and of any written reasons (ss 156(3), 158(4))`

GIVEN `I am the adult or another active party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was given notice of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I be given the decision`
`ss 156, 158 -- the decision` `I am the adult or another active party` `I was given notice of the hearing` MEANS
    IF `I am the adult or another active party`
    THEN `yes: you must be notified and given a copy of the decision as soon as practicable, and a copy of any written reasons (or told you may ask for them) (ss 156(2), (5), 158(3)); the tribunal may postpone this for up to 14 days at a time (s 157)`
    ELSE IF `I was given notice of the hearing`
         THEN `yes: you must be notified and given a copy of the decision as soon as practicable, and told you may ask for written reasons if it has none (s 156(2), (5)); you get the reasons themselves only on request (s 158(4))`
         ELSE `you are not a relevant person, but you may ask for a copy of the decision and of any written reasons (ss 156(3), 158(4))`

@export Must the tribunal give me its decision and reasons (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 156-158)?
GIVEN `I am the adult or another active party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the adult the matter concerns, or another active party in the proceeding?
      `I was given notice of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given notice of the hearing?
GIVETH A `Must I be given the decision`
DECIDE `Must I be given the decision question` IS
    `ss 156, 158 -- the decision` `I am the adult or another active party` `I was given notice of the hearing`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 163, 164 -- appeal`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 163(1): "An eligible person may appeal against a tribunal decision, other than a non-appellable decision, in a
-- proceeding as provided under the QCAT Act". (3): "eligible person-- (a) means-- (i) the person whose capacity for a
-- matter was under consideration in the proceeding; or (ii) the applicant in the proceeding; or (iii) a person proposed
-- for appointment by the proceeding; or (iv) a person whose power as guardian, administrator or attorney was changed or
-- removed by the tribunal decision; ... (viii) a person given leave to appeal by the appeal tribunal, or the Court of
-- Appeal". "non-appellable decision means a tribunal decision to make a limitation order under section 110." Limbs
-- (v)-(vii) (public guardian, public trustee, Attorney-General) and (b) (limitation orders) are officials or out of the
-- seat. s 164: after a postponement order under s 157, "the notice of appeal may be filed within 28 days after the later
-- of ... (a) the last day of the specified period or periods; (b) the date of the written reasons". The ordinary QCAT
-- appeal period (QCAT Act) is not deposited: no date is given without a postponement order.
DECLARE `Who wants to appeal` IS ONE OF
    `the person whose capacity was considered (me)`
    `the applicant`
    `the person proposed for appointment`
    `a person whose power as guardian, administrator or attorney the decision changed or removed`
    `a person given leave to appeal`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Can I appeal` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are an eligible person and may appeal under the QCAT Act, taken to be a party (s 163(1), (3))`
    `no: a decision to make a limitation order under s 110 cannot be appealed (s 163(2))`
    `no: you are not an eligible person unless the appeal tribunal or the Court of Appeal gives you leave (s 163(3))`

GIVEN `who appeals` IS A `Who wants to appeal`
      `the decision is a limitation order under s 110` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I appeal`
`s 163 -- appellant` `who appeals` `the decision is a limitation order under s 110` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a limitation order under s 110`
    THEN `no: a decision to make a limitation order under s 110 cannot be appealed (s 163(2))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `who appeals`
         WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: you are not an eligible person unless the appeal tribunal or the Court of Appeal gives you leave (s 163(3))`
         OTHERWISE `yes: you are an eligible person and may appeal under the QCAT Act, taken to be a party (s 163(1), (3))`

@export Can I appeal against the tribunal's guardianship or administration decision (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 163)?
GIVEN `who appeals` IS A `Who wants to appeal` @desc Who you are: the person whose capacity was considered; the applicant; the person proposed for appointment; a person whose power as guardian, administrator or attorney was changed or removed; a person given leave to appeal; or someone else
      `the decision is a limitation order under s 110` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a limitation order made before the hearing under s 110 (a non-publication or confidentiality order)?
GIVETH A `Can I appeal`
DECIDE `Can I appeal question` IS
    `s 163 -- appellant` `who appeals` `the decision is a limitation order under s 110`

GIVEN `the last day of the postponement` IS A DATE
      `the date of the written reasons` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 164 -- the last day to appeal after a postponement` `the last day of the postponement` `the date of the written reasons` MEANS
    28 `days after` (`the later of` `the last day of the postponement` `and` `the date of the written reasons`)

@export The tribunal postponed giving me its decision. By what day may I file my notice of appeal (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 164)?
GIVEN `the last day of the postponement` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period (or periods) for which the tribunal postponed giving you the decision (ISO 8601)
      `the date of the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc The date of the tribunal's written reasons (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Last day to appeal after a postponement question` IS
    `s 164 -- the last day to appeal after a postponement` `the last day of the postponement` `the date of the written reasons`

§ `Chapter 11 part 4: reporting abuse, and damages for a reprisal`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 247 -- protection for reporting abuse or a contravention`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 247(1): "A person is not liable, civilly, criminally or under an administrative process, for disclosing information
-- to an official if the person honestly believes, on reasonable grounds-- (a) the information tends to show-- (i) another
-- person has contravened this Act, the Powers of Attorney Act 1998 or the Public Guardian Act 2014; or (ii) an adult is,
-- or has been, the subject of neglect (including self-neglect), exploitation or abuse; or (b) the information would help
-- in the assessment or investigation of a complaint that [the same]." (2): absolute privilege in defamation;
-- confidentiality not breached; no disciplinary action. (3): "A person's liability for the person's own conduct is not
-- affected only because the person discloses it". (4): "official" is a QCAT registry officer, the public guardian or
-- staff or delegate, the public advocate or staff, or a community visitor (adult). An "if" condition: outside it s 247
-- gives no protection (JUST FALSE, worded "this section gives no protection on these facts").
DECLARE `Am I protected for reporting` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process for the disclosure; you have absolute privilege against defamation and breach no duty of confidence (s 247(1), (2)); your liability for your own conduct is unchanged (s 247(3))`
    `no: s 247 protects only a disclosure to an official: a QCAT registry officer, the public guardian or staff, the public advocate or staff, or a community visitor (s 247(4))`
    `no: s 247 gives no protection on these facts: it needs an honest belief, on reasonable grounds, that the information shows (or would help investigate a complaint of) a contravention, or neglect, exploitation or abuse of an adult (s 247(1))`

GIVEN `I disclosed to an official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I honestly believed on reasonable grounds it shows or would help investigate a contravention or abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Am I protected for reporting`
`s 247 -- whistleblowers' protection` `I disclosed to an official` `I honestly believed on reasonable grounds it shows or would help investigate a contravention or abuse` MEANS
    IF NOT `I disclosed to an official`
    THEN `no: s 247 protects only a disclosure to an official: a QCAT registry officer, the public guardian or staff, the public advocate or staff, or a community visitor (s 247(4))`
    ELSE IF `I honestly believed on reasonable grounds it shows or would help investigate a contravention or abuse`
         THEN `yes: you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process for the disclosure; you have absolute privilege against defamation and breach no duty of confidence (s 247(1), (2)); your liability for your own conduct is unchanged (s 247(3))`
         ELSE `no: s 247 gives no protection on these facts: it needs an honest belief, on reasonable grounds, that the information shows (or would help investigate a complaint of) a contravention, or neglect, exploitation or abuse of an adult (s 247(1))`

@export I reported that an adult with impaired capacity is being abused, neglected or exploited, or that an administrator broke the Act. Am I protected from being sued or punished for it (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 247)?
GIVEN `I disclosed to an official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose the information to an official: a QCAT registry officer, the public guardian or their staff or delegate, the public advocate or their staff, or a community visitor (adult)?
      `I honestly believed on reasonable grounds it shows or would help investigate a contravention or abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you honestly believe, on reasonable grounds, that the information shows (or would help investigate a complaint) that someone contravened the Act, the Powers of Attorney Act 1998 or the Public Guardian Act 2014, or that an adult was neglected, exploited or abused?
GIVETH AN `Am I protected for reporting`
DECIDE `Am I protected for reporting question` IS
    `s 247 -- whistleblowers' protection` `I disclosed to an official` `I honestly believed on reasonable grounds it shows or would help investigate a contravention or abuse`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 247A-247C -- damages for a reprisal`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 247A(1): "A person must not cause, or attempt or conspire to cause, detriment to another person because, or in the
-- belief that, the other person or someone else has disclosed or intends to disclose information under section
-- 247(1)." (5): "it is sufficient if the unlawful ground is a substantial ground for the act or omission". s 247B: an
-- offence, maximum 167 penalty units or 2 years imprisonment. s 247C(1): "A reprisal is a tort and a person who takes a
-- reprisal is liable in damages to any person who suffers detriment as a result." (2): any tort remedy, "including
-- exemplary damages". (3): tried in the Supreme or District Court "by a judge sitting without a jury". (5): even without
-- a prosecution. (6): "The Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 does not apply". s 247C has no time limit
-- of its own; the Limitation of Actions Act is not encoded here.
DECLARE `Can I sue for a reprisal` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the reprisal is a tort; you may sue the person who took it for damages, including exemplary damages, tried by a judge without a jury, whether or not they are prosecuted, and the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 does not apply (s 247C)`
    `no: s 247C gives damages only for a reprisal: detriment caused because of (as a substantial ground) a disclosure or intended disclosure under s 247(1) (s 247A)`
    `no: s 247C gives damages only to a person who suffers detriment as a result of the reprisal`

GIVEN `someone caused or tried to cause detriment, a substantial ground being a disclosure under s 247(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered detriment as a result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I sue for a reprisal`
`ss 247A, 247C -- damages for reprisal` `someone caused or tried to cause detriment, a substantial ground being a disclosure under s 247(1)` `I suffered detriment as a result` MEANS
    IF NOT `someone caused or tried to cause detriment, a substantial ground being a disclosure under s 247(1)`
    THEN `no: s 247C gives damages only for a reprisal: detriment caused because of (as a substantial ground) a disclosure or intended disclosure under s 247(1) (s 247A)`
    ELSE IF `I suffered detriment as a result`
         THEN `yes: the reprisal is a tort; you may sue the person who took it for damages, including exemplary damages, tried by a judge without a jury, whether or not they are prosecuted, and the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 does not apply (s 247C)`
         ELSE `no: s 247C gives damages only to a person who suffers detriment as a result of the reprisal`

@export Someone harmed me (for example sacked or threatened me) because I reported, or meant to report, abuse of an adult or a breach of the guardianship laws. Can I sue them for damages (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 247A-247C)?
GIVEN `someone caused or tried to cause detriment, a substantial ground being a disclosure under s 247(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did someone cause, or attempt or conspire to cause, detriment to someone, with a substantial reason being that a protected disclosure to an official was made or intended (by you or someone else)?
      `I suffered detriment as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer detriment as a result?
GIVETH A `Can I sue for a reprisal`
DECIDE `Can I sue for a reprisal question` IS
    `ss 247A, 247C -- damages for reprisal` `someone caused or tried to cause detriment, a substantial ground being a disclosure under s 247(1)` `I suffered detriment as a result`
